## 3. Preference Model Service
 
**Responsibility:** Maintains and evolves user's style preference vector through online learning from feedback signals.
 
### Core Capabilities
- Real-time preference vector updates
- Style archetype classification
- Temporal decay for evolving preferences
- Cold start handling via onboarding quiz
- Multi-dimensional preference tracking
### Architecture Flow
```
Feedback Events (Kafka)
        ↓
Event Processor (normalize, weight, timestamp)
        ↓
Feature Extractor (extract style tags from items)
        ↓
Vector Updater (online learning with temporal decay)
        ↓
Preference Vector Store (pgvector / Pinecone)
        ↓
Archetype Classifier (map to style archetypes)
```
 
### Preference Vector Schema
```typescript
interface UserPreferenceVector {
  user_id: string;
  version: number;
  updated_at: Date;
  
  // Multi-dimensional preference weights (0–1)
  colour_affinities: Record<string, number>;      // hue → weight
  pattern_weights: Record<string, number>;         // pattern_type → weight
  silhouette_prefs: Record<string, number>;        // silhouette → weight
  occasion_profile: Record<string, number>;        // occasion → weight
  brand_affinities: Record<string, number>;        // brand → weight
  
  // Style archetype probability distribution
  style_archetype_distribution: {
    minimalist: number;
    classic: number;
    streetwear: number;
    maximalist: number;
    athleisure: number;
  };
  
  // Learned scoring dimension weights
  dimension_weights: {
    colour: number;
    occasion: number;
    silhouette: number;
    novelty: number;
    preference: number;
  };
  
  confidence_score: number;  // 0–1, gates preference-heavy recommendations
}
```
 
### Training Signals
 
**Explicit signals:**
- Outfit ratings (1–5 stars post-wear)
- Item condition updates
- Outfit modification events
**Implicit signals:**
- Outfit wear events (positive)
- Outfit skip events (negative)
- Feed engagement (save > share > view > skip)
- Dwell time on recommendation detail view
### Cold Start Strategy
- Style onboarding quiz seeds initial vector (7 questions, 30 seconds)
- First 10 wear events: 50% personal preference + 50% archetype-average
- Confidence score gates preference-heavy recommendations until ≥0.60 threshold
### Data Ownership
- **Reads from:** Kafka `feedback.events`, PostgreSQL `feedback_events` table
- **Writes to:** Vector DB (embeddings), PostgreSQL `user_preferences` table
